                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: text: Explain the main ideas of class readings to absent students.
concept: Use examples to explain math concepts to peers.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can explain the main ideas from a reading about molas to an absent peer by pointing to colors and shapes (e.g., points to red and says, 'Molas are colorful.').
Can use examples to help peers understand mola patterns with visuals (e.g., points to a square and says, 'This is a square in the mola.').
Can help classmates count colors in molas to practice math (e.g., points to three colors and says 'one, two, three').</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
